# Databases. The app's own data lives in a data dir chosen at runtime
# (tmp-user-data/ in dev), never in the repo — anything matching here is real
# user content and must not be published. The -wal/-shm sidecars matter as
# much as the .db: a WAL holds recently-written pages.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
old_db_data/

# Secrets — none are committed and none should be. Every credential this
# app uses (Supabase URL/anon key, Google client id/secret) is entered in the
# app UI at runtime and stored in the local app_setting table, not in source.
#
# The Android release keystore moved to ZYDRAXYL/DraconDex-APK with the rest of
# the Flutter build; the keystore patterns below stay as a belt-and-braces guard
# against one ever being dropped in this tree by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
